-- ccc27-s745-6-review.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 745.6 to 745.64 (application for a reduction in the number of years of imprisonment
-- without eligibility for parole: who may apply and when, judicial screening, appeal, hearing by a jury, rules).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
-- Answers are `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (or a MAYBE of a type): JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING elsewhere.
-- "Within 90 days after the day X" is counted from X itself to the 90th day after it, both included (fork F-9 in NOTES.md).
-- Commencement days that the text does not state ("the day on which this subsection comes into force") are inputs.
-- Subsections 745.64(1) and (1.1) are machinery (rule-making power; Statutory Instruments Act): coverage table, inert, reason 2.

§ `Section 745.6 -- Application for judicial review`

-- Dates used below. The day five years after a day keeps its day and month and adds five to the year; a 29 February becomes 1 March (the date type has no 29 February in a non-leap year).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 745.6 the day five years after` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d) ((DATE_YEAR d) PLUS 5)

GIVEN d IS A DATE, days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 745.6 the day that many days after` MEANS Date ((DATE_DAY d) PLUS days) (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d)

-- "within 90 days after the day X": from X to the ninetieth day after it.
GIVEN day IS A DATE, start IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 745.6 the day is within ninety days after the start` MEANS
    (NOT (day LESS THAN start)) AND (NOT (day GREATER THAN (`s 745.6 the day that many days after` start 90)))

-- src:16149 | 745.6 (1) Subject to subsections (2) to (2.6), a person may apply, in writing, to the appropriate Chief Justice in the province in which their conviction took place for a reduction in the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole if the person
-- src:16150 | (a) has been convicted of murder or high treason;
-- src:16151 | (a.1) committed the murder or high treason before the day on which this paragraph comes into force;
-- src:16152 | (b) has been sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until more than fifteen years of their sentence has been served; and
-- src:16153 | (c) has served at least fifteen years of their sentence.
@ref s 745.6(1) (src:16149-16153)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of murder or high treason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person committed the murder or high treason before the day on which paragraph (1)(a.1) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole to which the person has been sentenced` IS A NUMBER
      `the years of their sentence the person has served` IS A NUMBER
      `the person has been convicted of more than one murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is in writing to the appropriate Chief Justice in the province in which the conviction took place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(1) the person may apply for a reduction in the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has been convicted of more than one murder`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (2), "A person who has been convicted of more than one murder may not make an application under subsection (1)"
        IF `the person has been convicted of murder or high treason` AND `the person committed the murder or high treason before the day on which paragraph (1)(a.1) comes into force`
           AND `the years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole to which the person has been sentenced` GREATER THAN 15
           AND `the years of their sentence the person has served` AT LEAST 15
           AND `the application is in writing to the appropriate Chief Justice in the province in which the conviction took place`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person may apply, in writing, ... if the person (a) has been convicted of murder or high treason; (a.1) committed the murder or high treason before the day ...; (b) has been sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until more than fifteen years of their sentence has been served; and (c) has served at least fifteen years of their sentence" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16155 | (2) A person who has been convicted of more than one murder may not make an application under subsection (1), whether or not proceedings were commenced in respect of any of the murders before another murder was committed.
@ref s 745.6(2) (src:16155)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of more than one murder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(2) the person may not make an application under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the person has been convicted of more than one murder`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the bar: "may not make an application", "whether or not proceedings were commenced in respect of any of the murders before another murder was committed"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who has been convicted of more than one murder"

-- src:16157 | (2.1) A person who is convicted of murder or high treason and who has served less than 15 years of their sentence on the day on which this subsection comes into force may, within 90 days after the day on which they have served 15 years of their sentence, make an application under subsection (1).
@ref s 745.6(2.1) (src:16157)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of murder or high treason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had served less than 15 years of their sentence on the day on which subsection (2.1) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person has served 15 years of their sentence` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(2.1) the person may make an application under subsection (1) on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is convicted of murder or high treason` AND `the person had served less than 15 years of their sentence on the day on which subsection (2.1) came into force`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is convicted of murder or high treason and who has served less than 15 years of their sentence on the day on which this subsection comes into force"
        IF `s 745.6 the day is within ninety days after the start` day `the day on which the person has served 15 years of their sentence`   -- "within 90 days" counted from the day itself to the 90th day after it, both included (fork F-9)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 90 days after the day on which they have served 15 years of their sentence" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a); a "may" with a period gate, listed, group (i))

-- src:16159 | (2.2) A person who is convicted of murder or high treason and who has served at least 15 years of their sentence on the day on which this subsection comes into force may make an application under subsection (1) within 90 days after
-- src:16160 | (a) the end of five years after the day on which the person was the subject of a determination made under subsection 745.61(4) or a determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) applies; or
-- src:16161 | (b) the day on which this subsection comes into force, if the person has not made an application under subsection (1).
@ref s 745.6(2.2) (src:16159-16161)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of murder or high treason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had served at least 15 years of their sentence on the day on which subsection (2.2) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the determination under subsection 745.61(4), or of the determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) applies` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which subsection (2.2) came into force` IS A DATE
      `the person has not made an application under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(2.2) the person may make an application under subsection (1) on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is convicted of murder or high treason` AND `the person had served at least 15 years of their sentence on the day on which subsection (2.2) came into force`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is convicted of murder or high treason and who has served at least 15 years of their sentence on the day on which this subsection comes into force"
        IF `inside paragraph (a)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `inside paragraph (b)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the day of the determination under subsection 745.61(4), or of the determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) applies` EQUALS NOTHING) AND (NOT (`the person has not made an application under subsection (1)`))
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither paragraph (a) nor paragraph (b) gives this person a window
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 90 days after (a) the end of five years after the day ...; or (b) the day on which this subsection comes into force, if the person has not made an application" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a); a "may" with a period gate, listed, group (i))
    WHERE
        `inside paragraph (a)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day of the determination under subsection 745.61(4), or of the determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) applies`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST d THEN `s 745.6 the day is within ninety days after the start` day (`s 745.6 the day five years after` d)   -- "within 90 days" counted from the day itself to the 90th day after it, both included (fork F-9)
        `inside paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `the person has not made an application under subsection (1)` AND `s 745.6 the day is within ninety days after the start` day `the day on which subsection (2.2) came into force`   -- "within 90 days" counted from the day itself to the 90th day after it, both included (fork F-9)

-- src:16163 | (2.3) Subsection (2.2) has no effect on a determination or decision made under subsection 745.61(3) or (5) or 745.63(3), (5) or (6) as it read immediately before the day on which this subsection comes into force. A person in respect of whom a time is set under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a) as it read immediately before that day may make an application under subsection (1) within 90 days after the end of that time.
@ref s 745.6(2.3) (src:16163)
GIVEN `the determination or decision was made under subsection 745.61(3) or (5) or 745.63(3), (5) or (6) as it read immediately before the day on which subsection (2.3) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(2.3) subsection (2.2) has an effect on the determination or decision` MEANS
    IF `the determination or decision was made under subsection 745.61(3) or (5) or 745.63(3), (5) or (6) as it read immediately before the day on which subsection (2.3) came into force`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2.2) has no effect on a determination or decision made under subsection 745.61(3) or (5) or 745.63(3), (5) or (6) as it read immediately before the day"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a determination or decision made under subsection 745.61(3) or (5) or 745.63(3), (5) or (6) as it read immediately before the day"

-- src:16163 | (2.3) Subsection (2.2) has no effect on a determination or decision made under subsection 745.61(3) or (5) or 745.63(3), (5) or (6) as it read immediately before the day on which this subsection comes into force. A person in respect of whom a time is set under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a) as it read immediately before that day may make an application under subsection (1) within 90 days after the end of that time.
@ref s 745.6(2.3) (src:16163)
GIVEN `the end of the time set under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a) as it read immediately before the day on which subsection (2.3) came into force` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(2.3) the person may make an application under subsection (1) on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the end of the time set under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a) as it read immediately before the day on which subsection (2.3) came into force`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person in respect of whom a time is set under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a) as it read immediately before that day"
    WHEN JUST e THEN
        IF `s 745.6 the day is within ninety days after the start` day e   -- "within 90 days" counted from the day itself to the 90th day after it, both included (fork F-9)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 90 days after the end of that time" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a); a "may" with a period gate, listed, group (i))

-- src:16165 | (2.4) If the person does not make an application in accordance with subsection (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3), as the case may be, they may make an application within 90 days after the day on which they have served a further five years of their sentence following the 90-day period referred to in that subsection, as the case may be.
@ref s 745.6(2.4) (src:16165)
GIVEN `the person made an application in accordance with subsection (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3), as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the 90-day period referred to in that subsection` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(2.4) the person may make an application under subsection (1) on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person made an application in accordance with subsection (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3), as the case may be`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the person does not make an application in accordance with subsection (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3)" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)
        IF `s 745.6 the day is within ninety days after the start` day (`s 745.6 the day five years after` `the last day of the 90-day period referred to in that subsection`)   -- "within 90 days" counted from the day itself to the 90th day after it, both included (fork F-9)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 90 days after the day on which they have served a further five years of their sentence following the 90-day period" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a); a "may" with a period gate, listed, group (i))

-- src:16167 | (2.5) A person who makes an application in accordance with subsection (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3), as the case may be, may make another application under subsection (1) within 90 days after
-- src:16168 | (a) the end of the time set under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a), if a time is set under that paragraph; or
-- src:16169 | (b) the end of five years after the day on which the person is the subject of a determination made under subsection 745.61(4) or a determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) applies, if the person is the subject of such a determination or conclusion.
@ref s 745.6(2.5) (src:16167-16169)
GIVEN `the person made an application in accordance with subsection (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3), as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the end of the time set under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the person is the subject of a determination made under subsection 745.61(4) or a determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) applies` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(2.5) the person may make another application under subsection (1) on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person made an application in accordance with subsection (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3), as the case may be`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who makes an application in accordance with subsection (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3), as the case may be" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)
        IF `inside paragraph (a)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `inside paragraph (b)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the end of the time set under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a)` EQUALS NOTHING) AND (`the day on which the person is the subject of a determination made under subsection 745.61(4) or a determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) applies` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no time has been set and the person is not the subject of such a determination, so neither paragraph gives a window
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 90 days after (a) the end of the time set ...; or (b) the end of five years after the day on which the person is the subject of a determination" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a); a "may" with a period gate, listed, group (i))
    WHERE
        `inside paragraph (a)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the end of the time set under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST e THEN `s 745.6 the day is within ninety days after the start` day e   -- "within 90 days" counted from the day itself to the 90th day after it, both included (fork F-9)
        `inside paragraph (b)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the person is the subject of a determination made under subsection 745.61(4) or a determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) applies`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST d THEN `s 745.6 the day is within ninety days after the start` day (`s 745.6 the day five years after` d)   -- "within 90 days" counted from the day itself to the 90th day after it, both included (fork F-9)

-- src:16171 | (2.6) A person who had made an application under subsection (1) as it read immediately before the day on which this subsection comes into force, whose application was finally disposed of on or after that day and who has then made a subsequent application may make a further application in accordance with subsection (2.5), if either paragraph (2.5)(a) or (b) is applicable.
@ref s 745.6(2.6) (src:16171)
GIVEN `the person had made an application under subsection (1) as it read immediately before the day on which subsection (2.6) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application was finally disposed of on or after that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has then made a subsequent application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `either paragraph (2.5)(a) or (b) is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(2.6) the person may make a further application in accordance with subsection (2.5)` MEANS
    IF `the person had made an application under subsection (1) as it read immediately before the day on which subsection (2.6) came into force` AND `the application was finally disposed of on or after that day`
       AND `the person has then made a subsequent application` AND `either paragraph (2.5)(a) or (b) is applicable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who had made an application ..., whose application was finally disposed of on or after that day and who has then made a subsequent application may make a further application in accordance with subsection (2.5), if either paragraph (2.5)(a) or (b) is applicable" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16172 | (2.7) The 90-day time limits for the making of any application referred to in subsections (2.1) to (2.5) may be extended by the appropriate Chief Justice, or his or her designate, to a maximum of 180 days if the person, due to circumstances beyond their control, is unable to make an application within the 90-day time limit.
@ref s 745.6(2.7) (src:16172)
GIVEN `the time limit is one of the 90-day time limits referred to in subsections (2.1) to (2.5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extension is by the appropriate Chief Justice, or his or her designate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, due to circumstances beyond their control, is unable to make an application within the 90-day time limit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended time limit, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(2.7) the time limit may be extended to the number of days` MEANS
    IF `the time limit is one of the 90-day time limits referred to in subsections (2.1) to (2.5)` AND `the extension is by the appropriate Chief Justice, or his or her designate`
       AND `the person, due to circumstances beyond their control, is unable to make an application within the 90-day time limit` AND `the extended time limit, in days` AT MOST 180
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be extended by the appropriate Chief Justice, or his or her designate, to a maximum of 180 days if the person, due to circumstances beyond their control, is unable to make an application within the 90-day time limit" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

DECLARE `s 745.6(2.8) relative` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.6(2.8) a parent, child, spouse or common-law partner of the victim`
    `s 745.6(2.8) another relative of the victim`
    `s 745.6(2.8) someone else`

-- src:16173 | (2.8) If a person convicted of murder does not make an application under subsection (1) within the maximum time period allowed by this section, the Commissioner of Correctional Service Canada, or his or her designate, shall immediately notify in writing a parent, child, spouse or common-law partner of the victim that the convicted person did not make an application. If it is not possible to notify one of the aforementioned relatives, then the notification shall be given to another relative of the victim. The notification shall specify the next date on which the convicted person will be eligible to make an application under subsection (1).
@ref s 745.6(2.8) (src:16173)
GIVEN `the person convicted of murder does not make an application under subsection (1) within the maximum time period allowed by the section` IS A BOOLEAN
      relative IS A `s 745.6(2.8) relative`
      `it is possible to notify a parent, child, spouse or common-law partner of the victim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(2.8) the Commissioner of Correctional Service Canada, or a designate, shall notify the relative in writing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person convicted of murder does not make an application under subsection (1) within the maximum time period allowed by the section`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person convicted of murder does not make an application under subsection (1) within the maximum time period allowed by this section" (a duty whose "if" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF relative EQUALS `s 745.6(2.8) a parent, child, spouse or common-law partner of the victim` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF relative EQUALS `s 745.6(2.8) another relative of the victim` THEN (IF `it is possible to notify a parent, child, spouse or common-law partner of the victim` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- "If it is not possible to notify one of the aforementioned relatives, then the notification shall be given to another relative of the victim"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names the victim's relatives and does not say that no one else is notified

-- src:16173 | (2.8) If a person convicted of murder does not make an application under subsection (1) within the maximum time period allowed by this section, the Commissioner of Correctional Service Canada, or his or her designate, shall immediately notify in writing a parent, child, spouse or common-law partner of the victim that the convicted person did not make an application. If it is not possible to notify one of the aforementioned relatives, then the notification shall be given to another relative of the victim. The notification shall specify the next date on which the convicted person will be eligible to make an application under subsection (1).
@ref s 745.6(2.8) (src:16173)
GIVEN `the notification is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification is given immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification specifies the next date on which the convicted person will be eligible to make an application under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.6(2.8) the notification meets the requirements of the subsection` MEANS
    IF `the notification is in writing` AND `the notification is given immediately` AND `the notification specifies the next date on which the convicted person will be eligible to make an application under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall immediately notify in writing ... The notification shall specify the next date on which the convicted person will be eligible to make an application"

DECLARE `s 745.6(3) Chief Justice` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.6(3)(a) the Chief Justice of the Ontario Court`
    `s 745.6(3)(b) the Chief Justice of the Superior Court`
    `s 745.6(3)(d) the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen's Bench`
    `s 745.6(3)(e) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    `s 745.6(3)(f) the Chief Justice of the Court of Appeal`

-- Paragraph (c) is shown repealed (line 16178), so no province is listed there: the thirteen provinces and territories are all covered by (a), (b), (d), (e) and (f).
-- src:16175 | (3) For the purposes of this section and sections 745.61 to 745.64, the appropriate Chief Justice is
-- src:16176 | (a) in relation to the Province of Ontario, the Chief Justice of the Ontario Court;
-- src:16177 | (b) in relation to the Province of Quebec, the Chief Justice of the Superior Court;
-- src:16178 | (c) [Repealed, 2026, c. 11, s. 44]
-- src:16179 | (d) in relation to the Provinces of New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen’s Bench;
-- src:16180 | (e) in relation to the Provinces of Nova Scotia, British Columbia, Prince Edward Island and Newfoundland and Labrador, the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court; and
-- src:16181 | (f) in relation to Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut, the Chief Justice of the Court of Appeal.
@ref s 745.6(3) (src:16175-16181)
GIVEN province IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A `s 745.6(3) Chief Justice`
`s 745.6(3) the appropriate Chief Justice` MEANS
    CONSIDER province
    WHEN Ontario THEN `s 745.6(3)(a) the Chief Justice of the Ontario Court`
    WHEN Quebec THEN `s 745.6(3)(b) the Chief Justice of the Superior Court`
    WHEN `New Brunswick` THEN `s 745.6(3)(d) the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen's Bench`
    WHEN Manitoba THEN `s 745.6(3)(d) the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen's Bench`
    WHEN Saskatchewan THEN `s 745.6(3)(d) the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen's Bench`
    WHEN Alberta THEN `s 745.6(3)(d) the Chief Justice of the Court of Queen's Bench`
    WHEN `Nova Scotia` THEN `s 745.6(3)(e) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `British Columbia` THEN `s 745.6(3)(e) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `Prince Edward Island` THEN `s 745.6(3)(e) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN `s 745.6(3)(e) the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN Yukon THEN `s 745.6(3)(f) the Chief Justice of the Court of Appeal`
    WHEN `Northwest Territories` THEN `s 745.6(3)(f) the Chief Justice of the Court of Appeal`
    WHEN Nunavut THEN `s 745.6(3)(f) the Chief Justice of the Court of Appeal`

§ `Section 745.61 -- Judicial screening`

DECLARE `s 745.63(1) criterion` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.63(1)(a) the character of the applicant`
    `s 745.63(1)(b) the applicant's conduct while serving the sentence`
    `s 745.63(1)(c) the nature of the offence for which the applicant was convicted`
    `s 745.63(1)(d) any information provided by a victim at the time of the imposition of the sentence or at the time of the hearing`
    `s 745.63(1)(e) any other matters that the judge considers relevant in the circumstances`
    `s 745.63(1) another criterion`

DECLARE `s 745.61(1) material` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.61(1)(a) the application`
    `s 745.61(1)(b) any report provided by the Correctional Service of Canada or other correctional authorities`
    `s 745.61(1)(c) any other written evidence presented to the Chief Justice or judge by the applicant or the Attorney General`
    `s 745.61(1) other material`

-- src:16183 | 745.61 (1) On receipt of an application under subsection 745.6(1), the appropriate Chief Justice shall determine, or shall designate a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction to determine, on the basis of the following written material, whether the applicant has shown, on a balance of probabilities, that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed:
-- src:16184 | (a) the application;
-- src:16185 | (b) any report provided by the Correctional Service of Canada or other correctional authorities; and
-- src:16186 | (c) any other written evidence presented to the Chief Justice or judge by the applicant or the Attorney General.
@ref s 745.61(1) (src:16183-16186)
GIVEN `an application under subsection 745.6(1) has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
      material IS A `s 745.61(1) material`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.61(1) the Chief Justice shall determine, on the basis of the material, whether the applicant has shown a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an application under subsection 745.6(1) has been received`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On receipt of an application under subsection 745.6(1), the appropriate Chief Justice shall determine" (a duty whose "on receipt" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF material EQUALS `s 745.61(1) other material` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "on the basis of the following written material" does not say "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16188 | (2) In determining whether the applicant has shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed, the Chief Justice or judge shall consider the criteria set out in paragraphs 745.63(1)(a) to (e), with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref s 745.61(2) (src:16188)
GIVEN criterion IS A `s 745.63(1) criterion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.61(2) the Chief Justice or judge shall consider the criterion` MEANS
    IF criterion EQUALS `s 745.63(1) another criterion`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the criteria set out in paragraphs 745.63(1)(a) to (e)" does not say "only"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16190 | (3) If the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed, the Chief Justice or judge may
-- src:16191 | (a) set a time, no earlier than five years after the date of the determination, at or after which the applicant may make another application under subsection 745.6(1); or
-- src:16192 | (b) decide that the applicant may not make another application under that subsection.
@ref s 745.61(3) (src:16190-16192)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the determination` IS A DATE
      `the time set` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.61(3)(a) the Chief Justice or judge may set the time` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed` AND (NOT (`the time set` LESS THAN (`s 745.6 the day five years after` `the date of the determination`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown ... the Chief Justice or judge may (a) set a time, no earlier than five years after the date of the determination" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16190 | (3) If the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed, the Chief Justice or judge may
-- src:16191 | (a) set a time, no earlier than five years after the date of the determination, at or after which the applicant may make another application under subsection 745.6(1); or
-- src:16192 | (b) decide that the applicant may not make another application under that subsection.
@ref s 745.61(3) (src:16190-16192)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.61(3)(b) the Chief Justice or judge may decide that the applicant may not make another application` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16194 | (4) If the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed but does not set a time for another application or decide that such an application may not be made, the applicant may make another application no earlier than five years after the date of the determination.
@ref s 745.61(4) (src:16194)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Justice or judge sets a time or decides that another application may not be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the determination` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.61(4) the applicant may make another application on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed`)) OR `the Chief Justice or judge sets a time or decides that another application may not be made`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has not shown ... but does not set a time for another application or decide that such an application may not be made" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)
        IF NOT (day LESS THAN (`s 745.6 the day five years after` `the date of the determination`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no earlier than five years after the date of the determination" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a); a "may" with a period gate, listed, group (i))

-- src:16196 | (5) If the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed, the Chief Justice shall designate a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction to empanel a jury to hear the application.
@ref s 745.61(5) (src:16196)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.61(5) the Chief Justice shall designate a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction to empanel a jury to hear the application` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Chief Justice or judge determines that the applicant has shown ..., the Chief Justice shall designate" (a duty whose "if" is unmet, fork F-3)

§ `Section 745.62 -- Appeal`

DECLARE `s 745.62(1) appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.62(1) the applicant`
    `s 745.62(1) the Attorney General`
    `s 745.62(1) someone else`

-- src:16198 | 745.62 (1) The applicant or the Attorney General may appeal to the Court of Appeal from a determination or a decision made under section 745.61 on any question of law or fact or mixed law and fact.
@ref s 745.62(1) (src:16198)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 745.62(1) appellant`
      `the appeal is from a determination or a decision made under section 745.61` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.62(1) the appellant may appeal to the Court of Appeal on any question of law or fact or mixed law and fact` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is from a determination or a decision made under section 745.61` AND NOT (appellant EQUALS `s 745.62(1) someone else`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The applicant or the Attorney General may appeal to the Court of Appeal from a determination or a decision made under section 745.61"

DECLARE `s 745.62(2) document` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.62(2) a document presented to the Chief Justice or judge who made the determination or decision`
    `s 745.62(2) any reasons for the determination or decision`
    `s 745.62(2) any other document that the Court of Appeal requires`
    `s 745.62(2) another document`

-- src:16200 | (2) The appeal shall be determined on the basis of the documents presented to the Chief Justice or judge who made the determination or decision, any reasons for the determination or decision and any other documents that the Court of Appeal requires.
@ref s 745.62(2) (src:16200)
GIVEN document IS A `s 745.62(2) document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.62(2) the appeal is determined on the basis of the document` MEANS
    IF document EQUALS `s 745.62(2) another document`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "on the basis of the documents ..., any reasons ... and any other documents that the Court of Appeal requires" does not say "only"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16202 | (3) Sections 673 to 696 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require.
@ref s 745.62(3) (src:16202)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.62(3) the provision applies to the appeal, with such modifications as the circumstances require` MEANS
    IF provision's `section` AT LEAST 673 AND provision's `section` AT MOST 696
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- "Sections 673 to 696": a decimal section between the two (for example 676.1 or 695.1) is read as inside the range (fork F-10)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 673 to 696 apply"

§ `Section 745.63 -- Hearing of application`

-- src:16204 | 745.63 (1) The jury empanelled under subsection 745.61(5) to hear the application shall consider the following criteria and determine whether the applicant’s number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole ought to be reduced:
-- src:16205 | (a) the character of the applicant;
-- src:16206 | (b) the applicant’s conduct while serving the sentence;
-- src:16207 | (c) the nature of the offence for which the applicant was convicted;
-- src:16208 | (d) any information provided by a victim at the time of the imposition of the sentence or at the time of the hearing under this section; and
-- src:16209 | (e) any other matters that the judge considers relevant in the circumstances.
@ref s 745.63(1) (src:16204-16209)
GIVEN criterion IS A `s 745.63(1) criterion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.63(1) the jury shall consider the criterion` MEANS
    IF criterion EQUALS `s 745.63(1) another criterion`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "shall consider the following criteria" does not say "only"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16208 | (d) any information provided by a victim at the time of the imposition of the sentence or at the time of the hearing under this section; and
@ref s 745.63(1)(d) (src:16208)
GIVEN `the person provides the information as the victim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person provides the information as an individual acting on the victim's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 victim: the purpose is section 745.63` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.63(1)(d) the information is information provided by a victim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person provides the information as the victim` THEN `s 2 victim: the purpose is section 745.63`
        IF `the person provides the information as an individual acting on the victim's behalf` THEN `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither the victim nor an individual acting on the victim's behalf

DECLARE `s 745.63(1.1) manner` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.63(1.1) orally`
    `s 745.63(1.1) in writing`
    `s 745.63(1.1) in another manner`

-- src:16211 | (1.1) Information provided by a victim referred to in paragraph (1)(d) may be provided either orally or in writing, at the discretion of the victim, or in any other manner that the judge considers appropriate.
@ref s 745.63(1.1) (src:16211)
GIVEN `the information is information provided by a victim referred to in paragraph (1)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      manner IS A `s 745.63(1.1) manner`
      `the judge considers the manner appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.63(1.1) the information may be provided in the manner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the information is information provided by a victim referred to in paragraph (1)(d)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information provided by a victim referred to in paragraph (1)(d)"
        IF manner EQUALS `s 745.63(1.1) orally` THEN JUST TRUE   -- "either orally or in writing, at the discretion of the victim"
        IF manner EQUALS `s 745.63(1.1) in writing` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the judge considers the manner appropriate` THEN JUST TRUE   -- "or in any other manner that the judge considers appropriate"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any other manner that the judge considers appropriate" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16214 | (3) The jury hearing an application under subsection (1) may determine that the applicant’s number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole ought to be reduced. The determination to reduce the number of years must be by unanimous vote.
@ref s 745.63(3) (src:16214)
GIVEN `the votes in favour of reducing the number of years` IS A NUMBER
      `the members of the jury` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.63(3) the determination to reduce the number of years is made by the vote the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the votes in favour of reducing the number of years` EQUALS `the members of the jury`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The determination to reduce the number of years must be by unanimous vote" (fork F-14)

-- src:16216 | (4) The applicant’s number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole is not reduced if
-- src:16217 | (a) the jury hearing an application under subsection (1) determines that the number of years ought not to be reduced;
-- src:16218 | (b) the jury hearing an application under subsection (1) concludes that it cannot unanimously determine that the number of years ought to be reduced; or
-- src:16219 | (c) the presiding judge, after the jury has deliberated for a reasonable period, concludes that the jury is unable to unanimously determine that the number of years ought to be reduced.
@ref s 745.63(4) (src:16216-16219)
GIVEN `the jury hearing an application under subsection (1) determines that the number of years ought not to be reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jury concludes that it cannot unanimously determine that the number of years ought to be reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the presiding judge, after the jury has deliberated for a reasonable period, concludes that the jury is unable to unanimously determine that the number of years ought to be reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.63(4) the applicant's number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole is not reduced` MEANS
    IF `the jury hearing an application under subsection (1) determines that the number of years ought not to be reduced` OR `the jury concludes that it cannot unanimously determine that the number of years ought to be reduced` OR `the presiding judge, after the jury has deliberated for a reasonable period, concludes that the jury is unable to unanimously determine that the number of years ought to be reduced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not reduced if (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." (the subsection's own question: none of the three is met)

DECLARE `s 745.63(5) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.63(5)(a) substitute a lesser number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole than that then applicable`
    `s 745.63(5)(b) terminate the ineligibility for parole`
    `s 745.63(5) another action`

-- src:16221 | (5) If the jury determines that the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole ought to be reduced, the jury may, by a vote of not less than two thirds of the members of the jury,
-- src:16222 | (a) substitute a lesser number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole than that then applicable; or
-- src:16223 | (b) terminate the ineligibility for parole.
@ref s 745.63(5) (src:16221-16223)
GIVEN `the jury determines that the number of years ought to be reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes in favour` IS A NUMBER
      `the members of the jury` IS A NUMBER
      action IS A `s 745.63(5) action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.63(5) the jury may take the action` MEANS
    IF `the jury determines that the number of years ought to be reduced` AND (`the votes in favour` TIMES 3) AT LEAST (`the members of the jury` TIMES 2) AND NOT (action EQUALS `s 745.63(5) another action`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the jury determines that the number of years ... ought to be reduced, the jury may, by a vote of not less than two thirds of the members of the jury, (a) substitute ...; or (b) terminate" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16225 | (6) If the applicant’s number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole is not reduced, the jury may
-- src:16226 | (a) set a time, no earlier than five years after the date of the determination or conclusion under subsection (4), at or after which the applicant may make another application under subsection 745.6(1); or
-- src:16227 | (b) decide that the applicant may not make another application under that subsection.
@ref s 745.63(6) (src:16225-16227)
GIVEN `the applicant's number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole is not reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the determination or conclusion under subsection (4)` IS A DATE
      `the time set` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.63(6)(a) the jury may set the time` MEANS
    IF `the applicant's number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole is not reduced` AND (NOT (`the time set` LESS THAN (`s 745.6 the day five years after` `the date of the determination or conclusion under subsection (4)`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the applicant's number of years ... is not reduced, the jury may (a) set a time, no earlier than five years after the date of the determination or conclusion" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16225 | (6) If the applicant’s number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole is not reduced, the jury may
-- src:16226 | (a) set a time, no earlier than five years after the date of the determination or conclusion under subsection (4), at or after which the applicant may make another application under subsection 745.6(1); or
-- src:16227 | (b) decide that the applicant may not make another application under that subsection.
@ref s 745.63(6) (src:16225-16227)
GIVEN `the applicant's number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole is not reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.63(6)(b) the jury may decide that the applicant may not make another application` MEANS
    IF `the applicant's number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole is not reduced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the applicant's number of years ... is not reduced" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16229 | (7) The decision of the jury under paragraph (6)(a) or (b) must be made by not less than two thirds of its members.
@ref s 745.63(7) (src:16229)
GIVEN `the votes in favour of the decision` IS A NUMBER
      `the members of the jury` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.63(7) the decision of the jury under paragraph (6)(a) or (b) is made by the vote the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (`the votes in favour of the decision` TIMES 3) AT LEAST (`the members of the jury` TIMES 2)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The decision of the jury under paragraph (6)(a) or (b) must be made by not less than two thirds of its members" (fork F-14)

-- src:16231 | (8) If the jury does not set a date on or after which another application may be made or decide that such an application may not be made, the applicant may make another application no earlier than five years after the date of the determination or conclusion under subsection (4).
@ref s 745.63(8) (src:16231)
GIVEN `the jury sets a date on or after which another application may be made, or decides that such an application may not be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the determination or conclusion under subsection (4)` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.63(8) the applicant may make another application on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the jury sets a date on or after which another application may be made, or decides that such an application may not be made`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the jury does not set a date on or after which another application may be made or decide that such an application may not be made" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)
        IF NOT (day LESS THAN (`s 745.6 the day five years after` `the date of the determination or conclusion under subsection (4)`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no earlier than five years after the date of the determination or conclusion" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a); a "may" with a period gate, listed, group (i))

§ `Section 745.64 -- Rules; territories`

DECLARE `s 745.64(2) court` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.64(2) the Court of Appeal of Yukon`
    `s 745.64(2) the Court of Appeal of the Northwest Territories`
    `s 745.64(2) the Court of Appeal of Nunavut`
    `s 745.64(2) the Supreme Court of Yukon`
    `s 745.64(2) the Supreme Court of the Northwest Territories`
    `s 745.64(2) the Nunavut Court of Justice`
    `s 745.64(2) another court`

-- src:16237 | (2) When the appropriate Chief Justice is designating a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction, for the purpose of a judicial screening under subsection 745.61(1) or to empanel a jury to hear an application under subsection 745.61(5), in respect of a conviction that took place in Yukon, the Northwest Territories or Nunavut, the appropriate Chief Justice may designate the judge from the Court of Appeal of Yukon, the Northwest Territories or Nunavut, or the Supreme Court of Yukon or the Northwest Territories or the Nunavut Court of Justice, as the case may be.
@ref s 745.64(2) (src:16237)
GIVEN `the appropriate Chief Justice is designating a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction, for the purpose of a judicial screening under subsection 745.61(1) or to empanel a jury to hear an application under subsection 745.61(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the province or territory in which the conviction took place` IS A `Province or territory`
      court IS A `s 745.64(2) court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.64(2) the appropriate Chief Justice may designate the judge from the court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the appropriate Chief Justice is designating a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction, for the purpose of a judicial screening under subsection 745.61(1) or to empanel a jury to hear an application under subsection 745.61(5)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the appropriate Chief Justice is designating a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction, for the purpose of a judicial screening ... or to empanel a jury ..." (a "when" gate on a "may": counts as "where" under ruling (b) as read in (c) of the 2026-11-05 delegated ruling; listed, group (i))
        IF NOT (elem (`the province or territory in which the conviction took place`) (LIST Yukon, `Northwest Territories`, Nunavut))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of a conviction that took place in Yukon, the Northwest Territories or Nunavut" (the same "when" clause; listed, group (i))
        IF `the court is one of the courts named for the territory` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may designate the judge from the Court of Appeal of Yukon, the Northwest Territories or Nunavut, or the Supreme Court of Yukon or the Northwest Territories or the Nunavut Court of Justice, as the case may be" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)
    WHERE
        `the court is one of the courts named for the territory` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the province or territory in which the conviction took place`
            WHEN Yukon THEN court EQUALS `s 745.64(2) the Court of Appeal of Yukon` OR court EQUALS `s 745.64(2) the Supreme Court of Yukon`
            WHEN `Northwest Territories` THEN court EQUALS `s 745.64(2) the Court of Appeal of the Northwest Territories` OR court EQUALS `s 745.64(2) the Supreme Court of the Northwest Territories`
            WHEN Nunavut THEN court EQUALS `s 745.64(2) the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` OR court EQUALS `s 745.64(2) the Nunavut Court of Justice`
            WHEN Ontario THEN FALSE
            WHEN Quebec THEN FALSE
            WHEN `Nova Scotia` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `British Columbia` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `Prince Edward Island` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `New Brunswick` THEN FALSE
            WHEN Manitoba THEN FALSE
            WHEN Saskatchewan THEN FALSE
            WHEN Alberta THEN FALSE
